Q: Dynamic Javascipt array manipulation A: <p>This code groups objects by a numeric property (like `age`) and collects the other property (`name`) into arrays. Works dynamically without hardcoding keys.</p>
<pre><code>
const data = [
  { name: 'Alice', age: 21 },
  { name: 'Henry', age: 20 },
  { name: 'Max', age: 20 },
  { name: 'Jane', age: 21 }
];

const result = Object.values(
  data.reduce((acc, obj) =&gt; {
    const [groupKey, otherKey] = Object.keys(obj).reduce((arr, k) =&gt; {
      if (typeof obj[k] === &quot;number&quot;) arr[0] = k;
      else arr[1] = k;
      return arr;
    }, []);

    if (!acc[obj[groupKey]]) acc[obj[groupKey]] = { [groupKey]: obj[groupKey], [otherKey]: [] };
    acc[obj[groupKey]][otherKey].push(obj[otherKey]);
    return acc;
  }, {})
);

console.log(result);
</code></pre>

Q: How to write custom schema validator functions for union types? A: <p>You can use <a href="https://angular.dev/api/forms/signals/applyWhenValue" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>applyWhenValue</code></a>, which conditionally applies the schema when the predicate is true:</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>export function validateWidget(path: SchemaPathTree&lt;Widget&gt;): void {
  applyWhenValue(path, (widget) =&gt; widget.type === 'A', validateWidgetA);
  applyWhenValue(path, (widget) =&gt; widget.type === 'B', validateWidgetB);
  applyWhenValue(path, (widget) =&gt; widget.type === 'C', validateWidgetC);
}
</code></pre>

Q: Bug for Animating against FocusState of TextField A: <p>It seems to be the insertion transitions that don't animate, the removal transitions do work.</p>
<p>A way to fix is to modify the transaction associated with the buttons using the <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/view/transaction(_:)" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>transaction(_:)</code></a> modifier. The documentation says:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Use this modifier to change or replace the animation used in a view</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It also has notes about correct usage:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Use this modifier on leaf views such as <code>Image</code> or <code>Button</code> rather than container views such as <code>VStack</code> or <code>HStack</code>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Here is how the example can be updated in this way. I tweaked the transition styles a bit too:</p>
<pre class="lang-swift prettyprint-override"><code>HStack {
    TextField(&quot;&quot;, text: .constant(&quot;&quot;))
        .focused($isFocused)
        .border(.red)

    if !isFocused {
        Button(&quot;Sort Button&quot;) {
            print(&quot;Sort clicked&quot;)
        }
        .transition(
            .opacity.animation(.easeInOut(duration: 1))
            .combined(with: .asymmetric(
                insertion: .push(from: .leading),
                removal: .push(from: .trailing)
            ))
        )
        .transaction { trans in
            trans.animation = .snappy(duration: 1)
        }
    } else {
        Button(&quot;Cancel&quot;) {
            isFocused = false
        }
        .transition(
            .opacity.animation(.easeInOut(duration: 1))
            .combined(with: .asymmetric(
                insertion: .push(from: .trailing),
                removal: .push(from: .leading)
            ))
        )
        .transaction { trans in
            trans.animation = .snappy(duration: 1)
        }
    }
}
.padding()
.geometryGroup()
.animation(.snappy(duration: 1), value: isFocused)
</code></pre>
